  "hints": [
    "Repeated digit sums preserve the number modulo 9.",
    "Positive multiples of 9 have digital root 9, while zero must remain 0.",
    "Return 0 for num==0; otherwise return 1+(num-1)%9.",
    "Subtracting one before the remainder maps each positive congruence class to the required range 1 through 9."
  ],
  "editorial": "Decimal place values are all congruent to one modulo nine, so replacing a number by its digit sum preserves its residue. Repetition ends at the unique representative from 1 through 9, except that input zero stays zero. The independent oracle performs the literal digit-summing process.",
